<title>AUSTRIA: BIATHLON-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BIATHLON-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ROSENAU-WINDISCHGARSTEN, Austria 1997-03-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results</p>
<p>at the European biathlon championships on Saturday:</p>
<p>Women's 7.5 km</p>
<p>1. Anna Stera (Poland) 23 minutes 06.0 seconds (no laps)</p>
<p>2. Tatiana Martynova (Russia) 23:14.2 (three laps)</p>
<p>3. Nathalie Santer (Italien) 23:30.5 (one lap)</p>
<p>4 equal. Steffi Kindt (Germany) 23:45.0 (two laps)</p>
<p>4  equal. Eija Salonen (Finland) 23:45.0 (no laps)</p>
<p>6. Katja Beer (Germany) 23:47.0 (one lap)</p>
<p>7. Yelena Shalina (Russia) 23:54.3 (two laps)</p>
<p>8. Pavlina Filipova (Bulgaria) 23:54.9 (two laps)</p>
<p>9. Martina Schwarzbacherova (Slovakia) 23:55.0 (one lap)</p>
<p>10. Sona Mihokova (Slovakia) 24:05.6 (two laps)</p>
<p>Men's 10 km</p>
<p>1. Andrei Padine (Russia) 28:24.7 (two laps)</p>
<p>2. Joze Poklukar (Slovenia) 28:26.6 (two laps)</p>
<p>3. Jaze Globocnik (Slovenia) 28:32.4 (one lap)</p>
<p>4. Ludwig Gredler (Austria) 28:32.6 (three laps)</p>
<p>5. Marco Morgenstern (Germany) 28:32.7 (two laps)</p>
<p>6. Einar Prucker (Italy) 28:33.5 (two laps)</p>
<p>7. Alexei Sidorov (Russia) 28:40.7 (one lap)</p>
<p>8. Ulf Karkoschka (Germany) 28:40.9 (one lap)</p>
<p>9. Alexander Popov (Belarus) 28:47.4 (no laps)</p>
<p>10. Ivan Masarik (Czech Republic) 28:53.8s (one lap)</p>
